Package: funresMech
Title: Mechanistic Functional Response Analysis with Simulation-Based Likelihood
Version: 1.2.0
Authors@R: 
    person('Segundo', 'Núñez-Campero', 
           email = 'segundo.nc@conicet.gov.ar', 
           role = c('aut', 'cre'))
Description: Fits mechanistic functional response models to
  experimental counts of hosts parasitized or prey consumed by
  simulation-based maximum likelihood (Okuyama 2012
  <doi:10.1016/j.biocontrol.2011.10.008>; Okuyama 2026 <doi:10.1111/jen.70148>).
  The probability distribution of the counts is obtained by simulating the
  search, encounter and handling process, with user-selectable distributions
  of search and handling times (built-in families or samplers written in R or
  C++), parasitoid (no host removal) or predator (prey removal) processes,
  and fixed or estimated parameters. Provides likelihood profiling of the
  density-scaling exponent, diagnostics of optimization and Monte Carlo
  reliability, screening of atypical trials, stochastic simulation and an
  interactive 'shiny' application with 'plotly' graphics and 'rmarkdown'
  reports. The simulation engine is implemented in C++ via 'Rcpp'.
